      "page_title": "asdict, astuple & replace",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What they do",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==asdict(obj)== gives {field name: value}, recursing into nested dataclasses, lists, tuples, dicts",
            "==astuple(obj)== recurses the same way, returns a tuple",
            "Both copy values with `copy.deepcopy`: slow on big objects",
            "==replace(obj, f=v)== returns a NEW instance with changes"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. asdict in action",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass",
            "class Line:",
            "    a: Point; b: Point",
            "asdict(Line(Point(0,0),Point(1,2)))",
            "# {'a':{'x':0,'y':0},'b':{...}}"
          ],
          "note": "nested Point became a dict too"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asdict(o, dict_factory=OrderedDict)` picks the mapping type",
            "`astuple(p)` on Point(1, 2) gives `(1, 2)`"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Path to JSON",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "import json",
            "json.dumps(asdict(u))",
            "# works: str, int, list, dict",
            "json.dumps(asdict(u),",
            "           default=str)  # datetime"
          ],
          "note": "all values must be JSON types"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Value",
            "json.dumps"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "str / int / list",
              "works"
            ],
            [
              "datetime",
              "needs default="
            ],
            [
              "Decimal",
              "needs default="
            ],
            [
              "Enum",
              "needs `.value`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. replace() for updates",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "@dataclass(frozen=True)",
            "class P: x: int; y: int",
            "p = P(1, 2)",
            "q = replace(p, x=9)",
            "# p -> P(1,2)  q -> P(9,2)"
          ],
          "note": "standard update tool for frozen"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`replace` calls ==__init__==, so __post_init__ and validation re-run",
            "`init=False` fields cannot be passed",
            "InitVar without default must be passed again, else **ValueError**"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. fields() and make_dataclass",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Attribute",
            "Holds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "name",
              "field name"
            ],
            [
              "type",
              "annotation"
            ],
            [
              "default",
              "plain default"
            ],
            [
              "default_factory",
              "factory callable"
            ],
            [
              "metadata",
              "mapping you attach"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "for f in fields(P):",
            "    print(f.name, f.type)",
            "C = make_dataclass(",
            "    'C', [('a', int)])  # dynamic"
          ],
          "note": "fields(cls) works on class or instance"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "asdict/astuple/replace never touch the original. Always capture the return value."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Deepcopy cost",
          "text": "asdict on a 10k-item list copies every item. Convert once, outside the loop."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Convert, copy, inspect"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Copy Mistakes & Their Fixes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Thinking `replace(p, x=9)` **mutates** p: it returns a copy; the original is unchanged",
            "Expecting asdict to return the live `__dict__`: it is a recursive ==converted copy==",
            "With `slots=True` there is no `__dict__` at all",
            "Calling asdict in a hot loop on large objects: deepcopy cost"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Fixing the mistakes",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "p = P(1, 2)",
            "replace(p, x=9)      # discarded",
            "p = replace(p, x=9)  # rebound",
            "d = asdict(p)        # new dict",
            "d['x'] = 0           # p unchanged"
          ],
          "note": "capture the return value"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Rebind the name: `p = replace(p, x=9)`",
            "Convert once, then reuse the dict",
            "On non-slots classes `vars(obj)` is the live dict",
            "Pass `dict_factory` to shape output in one step"
          ],
          "style": "check",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Side by side",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Returns",
            "Original"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "asdict",
              "dict",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "astuple",
              "tuple",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "replace",
              "new instance",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "fields",
              "Field tuple",
              "unchanged"
            ],
            [
              "is_dataclass",
              "bool",
              "unchanged"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Quick self-test",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "from dataclasses import *",
            "@dataclass",
            "class P: x: int; y: int",
            "p = P(1, 2)",
            "q = replace(p, x=9)",
            "print(p.x, q.x)  # 1 9"
          ],
          "note": "original stays untouched"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`replace` returns a new object every call",
            "Nested values inside are deep copies for asdict",
            "Shallow edits to `d` never reach `p`"
          ],
          "style": "checkbox"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Habit",
          "text": "Write `p = replace(p, ...)` on one line so the result is never dropped."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Convert, copy, inspect"
