      "page_title": "Dataclass vs NamedTuple vs TypedDict",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What each one is",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`typing.NamedTuple` = ==tuple subclass== with named fields, immutable, unpackable, indexable",
            "Dataclass = a normal class: **mutable** by default, not iterable, no indexing",
            "`TypedDict` = a plain `dict` at runtime; no methods, no instances of its own type"
          ],
          "style": "star",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "class P(NamedTuple):",
            "    x: int; y: int",
            "@dataclass",
            "class D: x: int; y: int",
            "class T(TypedDict): x: int; y: int"
          ],
          "note": "same record, three shapes"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Behaviour side by side",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Trait",
            "NamedTuple",
            "dataclass"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Mutability",
              "immutable",
              "mutable"
            ],
            [
              "Hashable",
              "yes (tuple)",
              "needs frozen"
            ],
            [
              "Ordering",
              "yes (tuple)",
              "order=True"
            ],
            [
              "Unpacking",
              "x, y = p",
              "no, add __iter__"
            ],
            [
              "Indexing",
              "p[0] works",
              "no"
            ],
            [
              "Defaults",
              "no factory",
              "default_factory"
            ],
            [
              "Inheritance",
              "very limited",
              "full support"
            ],
            [
              "JSON",
              "dict via _asdict()",
              "asdict()"
            ],
            [
              "Memory",
              "light, fast",
              "__dict__ / slots"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Equality and hashing",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "P(1, 2) == (1, 2)   # True",
            "D(1, 2) == (1, 2)   # False",
            "hash(P(1, 2))       # works",
            "hash(D(1, 2))       # TypeError",
            "{P(1, 2): 'ok'}     # valid key"
          ],
          "note": "tuple equality leaks across types"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "NamedTuple `P(1,2) == Q(1,2)` is True across unrelated types",
            "Dataclass `eq=True` kills `__hash__` unless frozen",
            "Dataclass needs `order=True`; tuple ordering is free"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Memory and speed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Kind",
            "Per-instance",
            "Create"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "NamedTuple",
              "tuple only",
              "fastest"
            ],
            [
              "slots=True dataclass",
              "close behind",
              "fast"
            ],
            [
              "plain dataclass",
              "has __dict__",
              "slower"
            ],
            [
              "TypedDict",
              "a dict",
              "dict speed"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Defaults and hooks",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "NamedTuple has no `field(default_factory=list)`; use `None` then fix",
            "Dataclass offers `__post_init__`, `InitVar`, and field options",
            "Subclassing a NamedTuple cannot add fields; dataclasses extend freely"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "TypedDict gotcha",
          "text": "`T(x=1,y=2)` returns a plain dict, so `isinstance(v, T)` raises TypeError."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "Tuple behaviour wanted? NamedTuple. Behaviour or state wanted? dataclass. Raw JSON shape? TypedDict."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "Pick the right record"
